# Nothing in this folder belongs on the web.
#
# The same net the shop system carries, and the panel needs it more.
#
# PANEL_DOC Section 4: "Document roots cannot leave public_html. Tested: cPanel
# silently created its own folder inside public_html and ignored the path typed
# in." So the ordinary outcome on this hosting is that a project ends up
# uploaded inside public_html, where everything beside `public/` is served too —
# including .env, which a browser will show as a page of plain text to anybody
# who guesses the URL.
#
# Section 4 also records finding exactly that on a real customer's install:
# Halabja-phone was serving its .env and its laravel.log to anyone.
#
# What is in the PANEL's .env is worse than one shop's:
#
#   - the database holding every customer, every licence and every payment
#   - PANEL_ADMIN_PASSWORD, and there is no second factor until somebody sets
#     one up
#   - PANEL_MAKER_* — an account that may CREATE and DROP DATABASE, which is
#     every shop on the account
#
# The real fix is `php artisan panel:public`, which puts the six files the web
# is allowed to see in their own folder and leaves this one outside it. This is
# the net for before that has been done, or if it is ever undone.
#
# Where the document root already points elsewhere, this file simply sits
# outside it and is never read. It costs nothing to leave in place.

<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    Require all denied
</IfModule>
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    Order allow,deny
    Deny from all
</IfModule>
